{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791561571,"nonce":"Sbxb6UIGHhZYYLq0Q9z++LN/r10=","title":"LoreSeries never sets prereq_base_commit: guard and regex use different trailer names","message":"**Report**\n\nFound while analysing find_base() on feature/find-base-precision.\n\nLoreSeries.add_patch() (src/b4/__init__.py:929-937 on master) tries to\nread a prerequisite base commit out of the cover letter:\n\n- the guard checks the body for `prerequisite-base-commit:`\n- the regex then searches for `^prerequisite-base-id:`\n\nA body can't match both, so `lser.prereq_base_commit` is never set. The\nconsumer in mbox.get_base_commit() (src/b4/mbox.py:72-76), which should\nprefer it over `base-commit:`, is dead code.\n\nBoth lines came in with 5d9e72e (\"ez: check that all dependencies can be\napplied\", 2024-03-28).\n\n**Impact**\n\nNone today: b4 prep never emits either trailer. A `base-commit:` entry in\nthe prerequisites (ez.py:2548) is folded into the plain `base-commit:` line\nof the cover letter. Only a hand-written `prerequisite-base-commit:` from\nanother tool would be ignored silently.","files":null}]}